{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Then let him count the years of his sale.</b> \"How many years were there until the Jubilee? So many. And for how much did I sell it to you? For so much. You were going to return it at the Jubilee — so you were buying the number of harvests according to the reckoning of each year. You ate from it three or four years — deduct their value from the total and take the rest.\" And this is ״וְהֵשִׁיב אֶת הָעֹדֵף״ — he returns the excess in the purchase price, for the produce that he consumed, and gives it to the buyer." "<b>To the man to whom he sold it.</b> This is the seller, who comes to redeem it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:21.641470715Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}